 "notes": "Photophilic (g_aee=0) result, Fig.1 (T_RH=5 MeV, g_agg_constraints.pdf), the headline result (abstract leads with g_agg<=8.1e-14 GeV^-1 at 10 keV; my envelope gives 8.15e-14 at 10 keV, calibration verified). Curve is the LOWER boundary (exclusion reach in coupling) of the union of the paper own irreducible-freeze-in constraints: CRB (green), X-ray (orange/mustard, recast local DM-decay searches), CMB anisotropies (velvet) and CMB spectral distortions SD (dark gray). Light-gray astrophysical regions (HB stars, SN1987A, Solar Basin) are NOT the paper own limits and are excluded. The disconnected dark-gray BBN blob (m~4e3-2e4 keV) is for T_RH=10 MeV, not 5 MeV, and does not affect the low-coupling reach; excluded. The excluded region is actually a band; only its lower edge (the strong new reach) is reported as g(m). X-ray tip reaches ~2e-16 near 1.6 MeV; CMB branch reaches ~4e-16 near 2e4 keV. Extracted from vector fills of the arXiv figure via pymupdf get_drawings with tick-calibrated log axes. Confidence level not stated by paper; 0.95 assumed. Density: relic freeze-in abundance argument, not a local-DM-density haloscope, so no dm_density rescaling applies (null).",
